 ## Subtopics
 
-### BSP-XMPVO
-An algorithm that improves XMPVO results by building a view-independent BSP tree of the exterior faces to reduce the number of ray shooting queries needed [S2, unofficial]. It augments MPVO ordering using binary space partitions on boundary elements [S2, unofficial]. Runtime is $O(n + bp)$, where $p$ is the size of a small subset of exterior cells [S2, unofficial]. However, building the BSP structure is very slow, and the tree can become deep and unbalanced, leading to $O(b)$ cost per search and $O(b^2)$ overall flavor [S2, unofficial]. Results are orders of magnitude better than previous exact methods, but SXMPVO is faster and easier to implement than BSP-XMPVO [S2, S3, unofficial].
+### [BSP-XMPVO](1160-bsp-xmpvo.md)
+An algorithm that improves XMPVO results by building a view-independent BSP tree of the exterior faces to reduce the number of ray shooting queries needed. It augments MPVO ordering using binary space partitions on boundary elements. Runtime is $O(n + bp)$, where $p$ is the size of a small subset of exterior cells. However, building the BSP structure is very slow, and the tree can become deep and unbalanced, leading to $O(b)$ cost per search and $O(b^2)$ overall flavor. Results are orders of magnitude better than previous exact methods, but SXMPVO is faster and easier to implement than BSP-XMPVO.
 
